{"type":"message","id":"5bc5092e","parentId":"3ec269af","timestamp":"2026-04-17T11:12:14.617Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good picture of the task status. Let me now update my heartbeat in the bitable and check for overdue tasks. Let me get more records to see the full picture, and also check the timestamps more carefully.\n\nCurrent time: 2026-04-17T11:11:00 UTC\n\nLet me check for any records that need to be marked as Dead (updated > 60 minutes ago). The current timestamp would be around 177 586 866 0000 (April 17, 2026 in milliseconds). Let me calculate: April 17, 2026 11:11 UTC = 1776421860000 ms roughly.\n \nI'm looking at the task records and noticing something odd with the timestamps. The \"最后心跳\" values like 1744877460000 don't match the current date in April 2026, which suggests there might be a time zone or epoch issue with how the dates are being recorded.\n\nLooking at the bitable more carefully, I see the \"状态\" field already contains the Dead designation I was about to flag, so these tasks appear to already be marked correctly. My approach should be to document my own heartbeat in the bitable for this check cycle, then compile the summary for the shared pool. The active tasks I should highlight include the weekly recurring task and another one marked as 进行中, while the bulk of the worklog entries seem to be historical or completed checks.\n\nNow I need to find the actual heartbeat field in the bitable structure and update it with the current timestamp. Since the existing records don't have a \"最后心跳\" field populated, I should look for where that timestamp would go or consider creating a new status record for this check-in. Updating the heartbeat in the shared pool work progress table, then I need to verify if there are any overdue tasks based on the 60-minute threshold from the last heartbeat recorded on April 17, 2026 around 11:11 UTC. So a task should be marked Dead if its last heartbeat is more than 60 minutes before the current check time of 1746429060000, which means anything before 1746428460000 would qualify. Looking at the records I have, most show Dead status already, so I need to check what the actual last heartbeat times are in the shared pool bitable to see if any new tasks should be flagged.\n\nI'm realizing the timestamps in the \"最后心跳\" field appear to be in seconds rather than milliseconds—they're showing values like 1744877460000, which actually corresponds to January 2026, not April. This suggests the system has been running for about 100 days, which aligns with the records starting around April 14. Let me recalculate the time thresholds using seconds instead: 60 minutes would be 3600 seconds, so I need to convert the current time and check what's actually overdue. I'm realizing there's a unit mismatch—the field stores milliseconds (1744877460000) but my calculation treats it as seconds, which throws off the comparison by a factor of 1000. Let me recalculate the deadline by converting everything consistently: 60 minutes is 3600 seconds, so the threshold should be 1746429060 seconds, and I need to compare that against the stored millisecond value divided by 1000.\n\nBut wait, even with that correction, 1744877460 seconds converts to January 2026, which contradicts the creation timestamp from April 2026—that doesn't add up. I'm wondering if these timestamps are actually in a different format or if there's something else going on with how the dates are being recorded.\n\nLet me just move forward with documenting my heartbeat and summarizing the current state. I'll record a new entry with the check time of 2026-04-17 11:11 UTC and note the key metrics: around 20 total tasks with 3 marked as Dead, 1 in progress, and the rest either completed or pending execution.\n\nNow I need to update the record with my current heartbeat and insert this new check entry into the bitable."},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me update my heartbeat and record the check in the shared pool:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_18poddz0reaj_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_field","arguments":{"action":"list","app_token":"ZJ8obBGrSaO9rjsXPvhc1TdYngd","table_id":"tblt4LNepLsvevNr"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776424311775,"responseId":"06314877006f13596433c378d281b606"}}
